INSERT INTO `course_assessments` VALUES (2,'GRADE 7 — PRE-TEST (The School Repair Project) ','Pre-Test','Frustration',7,'<p>When the rainy season began, students at Mabini National High School noticed that several parts of their classroom needed repair. Some windows could no longer close properly, and rainwater entered through a small hole in the roof. The problem became especially difficult during afternoon classes.</p>\r\n<p>Their class adviser, Mr. Santos, asked the students to think of ways they could help. He explained that they could not perform dangerous repairs themselves, but they could help keep the classroom clean and organize materials for the repair workers.</p>\r\n<p>The students divided themselves into groups. One group listed the damaged parts of the room. Another group collected books and learning materials that needed to be moved away from the leaking area. A third group cleaned the classroom after the repair workers finished each day.</p>\r\n<p>The project took several weeks because some materials had to be ordered. Although the students became tired, they continued helping. They discovered that even simple tasks became easier when everyone worked together.</p>\r\n<p>When the repairs were finally completed, the classroom was safer and more comfortable. The students were proud of their work. They realized that taking responsibility did not always mean doing everything themselves. Sometimes, it meant knowing how to help safely and responsibly.</p>','[{\"type\":\"multichoice\",\"question\":\"What problem did the students notice in their classroom?\",\"options\":[\"The classroom had too many chairs.\",\"Several parts of the classroom needed repair.\",\"The students did not have enough books.\",\"The classroom was too small.\"],\"correct\":\"1\"},{\"type\":\"multichoice\",\"question\":\"Why did rainwater enter the classroom?\",\"options\":[\"A window was broken.\",\"The door was missing.\",\"There was a hole in the roof.\",\"The floor was damaged.\"],\"correct\":\"2\"},{\"type\":\"multichoice\",\"question\":\"What did Mr. Santos ask the students to do?\",\"options\":[\"Repair the roof themselves.\",\"Leave the classroom permanently.\",\"Think of safe ways they could help.\",\"Ask another school for a classroom.\"],\"correct\":\"2\"},{\"type\":\"multichoice\",\"question\":\"What did the first group do?\",\"options\":[\"Cleaned the windows.\",\"Listed the damaged parts.\",\"Repaired the roof.\",\"Ordered construction materials.\"],\"correct\":\"1\"},{\"type\":\"multichoice\",\"question\":\"Why were some materials moved?\",\"options\":[\"They were going to be sold.\",\"They were old and useless.\",\"They needed protection from the leaking area.\",\"The students wanted new materials.\"],\"correct\":\"2\"},{\"type\":\"multichoice\",\"question\":\"What made the project take several weeks?\",\"options\":[\"The students refused to help.\",\"The classroom was too large.\",\"Some materials had to be ordered.\",\"The teacher was absent.\"],\"correct\":\"2\"},{\"type\":\"multichoice\",\"question\":\"What did the students learn from the project?\",\"options\":[\"Working alone is always better.\",\"Responsibility includes helping safely.\",\"Repairs should always be done by students.\",\"Classroom projects are unnecessary.\"],\"correct\":\"1\"},{\"type\":\"multichoice\",\"question\":\"Which word best describes the students?\",\"options\":[\"Careless\",\"Uncooperative\",\"Responsible\",\"Impatient\"],\"correct\":\"2\"},{\"type\":\"multichoice\",\"question\":\"What is the main idea of the passage?\",\"options\":[\"Students should repair school buildings.\",\"Teamwork can help students contribute responsibly to a school project.\",\"Teachers should do all classroom repairs.\",\"Rainy weather makes studying impossible.\"],\"correct\":\"1\"},{\"type\":\"multichoice\",\"question\":\"What can be inferred from the passage?\",\"options\":[\"The students learned that cooperation made the work easier.\",\"The students disliked their classroom.\",\"The repair workers refused to work.\",\"The school planned to close.\"],\"correct\":\"0\"}]','Published',NULL,'2026-10-08 04:29:35','2026-10-08 14:01:48'),(3,'GRADE 7 — POST-TEST (The School Recycling Program)','Post-Test','Frustration',7,'<p>Students at San Isidro National High School noticed that large amounts of paper and plastic were being thrown away every day. Their science teacher, Ms. Reyes, suggested creating a recycling program.</p>\r\n<p>The students first examined the school\'s waste bins. They discovered that many recyclable materials were mixed with food waste and other garbage. The students decided to place labeled containers in different areas of the school.</p>\r\n<p>Each class was assigned a responsibility. Some students collected recyclable materials, while others recorded the amount gathered each week. The science club also taught students how to separate paper, plastic, and other materials properly.</p>\r\n<p>During the first few weeks, the program did not work perfectly. Some students continued putting garbage into the wrong containers. Instead of giving up, the organizers placed clearer signs near the bins and reminded students about the purpose of the program.</p>\r\n<p>After several months, the amount of recyclable waste increased. The school also produced less mixed garbage. The students realized that successful environmental projects required patience, cooperation, and regular effort.</p>','[{\"type\":\"multichoice\",\"question\":\"What problem did the students notice?\",\"options\":[\"Too many students were absent.\",\"Large amounts of recyclable material were being thrown away.\",\"The school had no science teacher.\",\"The classrooms had too many containers.\"],\"correct\":\"1\"},{\"type\":\"multichoice\",\"question\":\"What did the students discover when they examined the waste bins?\",\"options\":[\"They were completely empty.\",\"All waste was properly separated.\",\"Recyclable materials were mixed with other garbage.\",\"Students were not using the bins.\"],\"correct\":\"2\"},{\"type\":\"multichoice\",\"question\":\"What did the students place around the school?\",\"options\":[\"New classrooms\",\"Labeled recycling containers\",\"More desks\",\"Water tanks\"],\"correct\":\"1\"},{\"type\":\"multichoice\",\"question\":\"What did some students record?\",\"options\":[\"The number of teachers\",\"The amount of recyclable materials collected\",\"The number of classrooms\",\"The students\' test scores\"],\"correct\":\"1\"},{\"type\":\"multichoice\",\"question\":\"What problem occurred during the first few weeks?\",\"options\":[\"Students used the wrong containers.\",\"The recycling bins disappeared.\",\"The science club stopped meeting.\",\"There was no recyclable material.\"],\"correct\":\"0\"},{\"type\":\"multichoice\",\"question\":\"How did the organizers respond to the problem?\",\"options\":[\"They cancelled the program.\",\"They removed all the containers.\",\"They added clearer signs and reminders.\",\"They punished every student.\"],\"correct\":\"2\"},{\"type\":\"multichoice\",\"question\":\"What happened after several months?\",\"options\":[\"Recyclable waste increased and mixed garbage decreased.\",\"The recycling program was abandoned.\",\"Students stopped collecting materials.\",\"The school produced more garbage.\"],\"correct\":\"0\"},{\"type\":\"multichoice\",\"question\":\"Which quality helped the students continue the program?\",\"options\":[\"Laziness\",\"Patience\",\"Fear\",\"Competition\"],\"correct\":\"1\"},{\"type\":\"multichoice\",\"question\":\"What is the main idea?\",\"options\":[\"Recycling projects are difficult and useless.\",\"Environmental programs can succeed through cooperation and continuous effort.\",\"Students should avoid using plastic.\",\"Schools should remove all waste bins.\"],\"correct\":\"1\"},{\"type\":\"multichoice\",\"question\":\"What can be inferred from the passage?\",\"options\":[\"The students improved the program by responding to problems.\",\"The program succeeded immediately.\",\"The teacher did all the work.\",\"The students were not interested in recycling.\"],\"correct\":\"0\"}]','Published',NULL,'2026-10-08 04:29:35','2026-10-08 06:29:09'),(4,'GRADE 8 — PRE-TEST (The Importance of Mangroves)','Pre-Test','Instructional',8,'<p>Along many coastal communities in the Philippines, mangrove forests grow where land meets the sea. These trees are specially adapted to survive in salty water and muddy soil. Although they may look ordinary, mangroves provide important benefits to both people and wildlife.</p>\n<p>The tangled roots of mangrove trees help reduce the force of waves. During strong storms, these roots can help protect coastal areas from erosion. Mangrove forests also provide shelter for young fish, crabs, and other animals.</p>\n<p>Mangroves are also important to local communities. Fishermen may depend on healthy coastal ecosystems for their livelihood. When mangrove forests are damaged, the number of fish and other marine animals may decrease.</p>\n<p>Unfortunately, some mangrove areas have been removed to make space for buildings, roads, and other developments. Pollution can also harm these ecosystems.</p>\n<p>Many communities now participate in mangrove restoration projects. Volunteers plant young mangrove trees and protect existing forests. These efforts demonstrate that protecting nature can also protect people\'s livelihoods and communities.</p>','[{\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"Where do mangroves commonly grow?\", \"options\": [\"In deserts\", \"Where land meets the sea\", \"On mountain peaks\", \"In dry grasslands\"], \"correct\": \"1\"}, {\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"What helps mangroves survive in coastal areas?\", \"options\": [\"Their ability to live in salty water and muddy soil\", \"Their ability to grow without water\", \"Their ability to live only in forests\", \"Their ability to survive without sunlight\"], \"correct\": \"0\"}, {\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"How can mangrove roots help coastal communities?\", \"options\": [\"They increase the force of waves.\", \"They reduce wave force and erosion.\", \"They remove all seawater.\", \"They prevent rainfall.\"], \"correct\": \"1\"}, {\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"What animals can find shelter in mangrove forests?\", \"options\": [\"Young fish and crabs\", \"Mountain goats\", \"Eagles only\", \"Farm animals\"], \"correct\": \"0\"}, {\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"Why are mangroves important to fishermen?\", \"options\": [\"They provide buildings for fishermen.\", \"They support coastal ecosystems where fish can live.\", \"They make boats unnecessary.\", \"They prevent all storms.\"], \"correct\": \"1\"}, {\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"What is one cause of mangrove destruction?\", \"options\": [\"Too much rainfall\", \"Building and development\", \"Too many fish\", \"Strong sunlight\"], \"correct\": \"1\"}, {\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"What is mangrove restoration?\", \"options\": [\"Removing all mangrove trees\", \"Planting and protecting mangrove forests\", \"Building roads through forests\", \"Moving coastal communities\"], \"correct\": \"1\"}, {\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"What is the author\'s main purpose?\", \"options\": [\"To explain the importance of mangroves\", \"To teach readers how to build boats\", \"To describe different kinds of fish\", \"To explain how to become a fisherman\"], \"correct\": \"0\"}, {\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"Which statement is supported by the passage?\", \"options\": [\"Mangroves are useful only to animals.\", \"Damaging mangroves can affect both nature and people.\", \"Mangroves cannot survive near the sea.\", \"Communities should remove mangroves.\"], \"correct\": \"1\"}, {\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"What can be inferred from the passage?\", \"options\": [\"Protecting mangroves can benefit both communities and ecosystems.\", \"Mangrove restoration has no effect on communities.\", \"Coastal communities do not depend on nature.\", \"Mangrove forests are dangerous to fish.\"], \"correct\": \"0\"}]','Published',NULL,'2026-10-08 04:29:35','2026-10-08 12:20:00'),(5,'GRADE 8 — POST-TEST (Protecting Coral Reefs)','Post-Test','Instructional',8,'<p>Coral reefs are among the most diverse ecosystems in the ocean. They provide shelter and food for many kinds of marine animals. Although coral reefs cover only a small part of the ocean floor, they support a large variety of life.</p>\n<p>Healthy coral reefs can also benefit coastal communities. They can help reduce the energy of waves before those waves reach shore. Reefs also support fishing and tourism, which provide income for many people.</p>\n<p>However, coral reefs face several threats. Pollution, destructive fishing practices, rising sea temperatures, and careless tourism can damage them. When corals become stressed, they may lose the tiny organisms that give them much of their color. This process is known as coral bleaching.</p>\n<p>Scientists and communities are working together to protect coral reefs. Some projects establish marine protected areas where fishing and other activities are limited. Other projects teach tourists how to visit reefs without damaging them.</p>\n<p>Protecting coral reefs requires cooperation. Governments, communities, tourists, and individuals all have a role in keeping marine ecosystems healthy.</p>','[{\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"What are coral reefs?\", \"options\": [\"Desert ecosystems\", \"Diverse marine ecosystems\", \"Freshwater lakes\", \"Mountain forests\"], \"correct\": \"1\"}, {\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"Why are coral reefs important to marine animals?\", \"options\": [\"They provide food and shelter.\", \"They prevent animals from swimming.\", \"They remove seawater.\", \"They produce freshwater.\"], \"correct\": \"0\"}, {\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"How can coral reefs benefit coastal communities?\", \"options\": [\"They eliminate storms completely.\", \"They support fishing and tourism.\", \"They prevent people from visiting beaches.\", \"They make boats unnecessary.\"], \"correct\": \"1\"}, {\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"Which is a threat to coral reefs?\", \"options\": [\"Responsible tourism\", \"Destructive fishing\", \"Marine protection\", \"Scientific research\"], \"correct\": \"1\"}, {\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"What happens during coral bleaching?\", \"options\": [\"Corals become healthier.\", \"Corals lose the organisms that give them color.\", \"Fish leave the ocean permanently.\", \"Coral reefs turn into forests.\"], \"correct\": \"1\"}, {\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"What is one way communities protect reefs?\", \"options\": [\"Establishing marine protected areas\", \"Increasing destructive fishing\", \"Removing all marine animals\", \"Allowing unlimited pollution\"], \"correct\": \"0\"}, {\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"Why do scientists teach tourists about responsible behavior?\", \"options\": [\"To encourage tourists to damage reefs\", \"To reduce harmful activities around reefs\", \"To stop all tourism\", \"To prevent people from swimming\"], \"correct\": \"1\"}, {\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"What is the main idea?\", \"options\": [\"Coral reefs are valuable ecosystems that require protection.\", \"Coral reefs are dangerous places.\", \"Tourism always damages reefs.\", \"Fishing should be completely stopped.\"], \"correct\": \"0\"}, {\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"What does the passage suggest about protecting coral reefs?\", \"options\": [\"Only scientists can protect them.\", \"Cooperation among different groups is necessary.\", \"Tourists have no responsibility.\", \"Governments cannot help.\"], \"correct\": \"1\"}, {\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"What can be inferred?\", \"options\": [\"Human activities can affect the health of marine ecosystems.\", \"Coral reefs are unaffected by pollution.\", \"Marine ecosystems do not benefit people.\", \"Coral bleaching always improves reefs.\"], \"correct\": \"0\"}]','Published',NULL,'2026-10-08 04:29:35','2026-10-08 12:20:00'),(6,'GRADE 9 — PRE-TEST (Artificial Intelligence in the Classroom)','Pre-Test','Frustration',9,'<p>Artificial intelligence, or AI, is becoming more common in schools. Some teachers use AI-powered tools to help create learning materials, provide explanations, or give students additional practice.</p>\n<p>One possible benefit of AI is that it can provide immediate feedback. For example, a student practicing grammar may receive information about mistakes without waiting for the next class meeting. AI tools can also present information in different ways depending on the learner\'s needs.</p>\n<p>However, AI should not replace teachers. A computer program may provide an answer, but it cannot completely understand a student\'s emotions, personal experiences, or difficulties. Teachers also help students develop communication, judgment, and social skills.</p>\n<p>There are also concerns about accuracy and responsible use. AI systems can sometimes provide incorrect information. Students who depend too heavily on AI may also fail to develop their own problem-solving skills.</p>\n<p>For these reasons, schools should teach students how to use AI responsibly. AI can be a useful educational tool when it supports learning rather than replacing the effort and thinking required from students.</p>','[{\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"What does AI stand for?\", \"options\": [\"Automatic Information\", \"Artificial Intelligence\", \"Advanced Internet\", \"Applied Instruction\"], \"correct\": \"1\"}, {\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"How can AI provide immediate feedback?\", \"options\": [\"By giving information about mistakes quickly\", \"By replacing teachers\", \"By removing assignments\", \"By preventing students from practicing\"], \"correct\": \"0\"}, {\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"What is one possible benefit of AI?\", \"options\": [\"It can provide additional learning practice.\", \"It eliminates the need for teachers.\", \"It guarantees correct information.\", \"It prevents students from making mistakes.\"], \"correct\": \"0\"}, {\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"Why should AI not completely replace teachers?\", \"options\": [\"Teachers can understand students in ways AI cannot.\", \"Teachers cannot use technology.\", \"AI cannot provide information.\", \"Teachers do not need technology.\"], \"correct\": \"0\"}, {\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"What is one concern about AI?\", \"options\": [\"It can sometimes provide incorrect information.\", \"It always gives correct answers.\", \"It cannot process information.\", \"It cannot be used in education.\"], \"correct\": \"0\"}, {\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"What may happen if students depend too heavily on AI?\", \"options\": [\"Their problem-solving skills may not develop properly.\", \"They will automatically become better readers.\", \"They will no longer need education.\", \"They will understand every subject perfectly.\"], \"correct\": \"0\"}, {\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"What does the author recommend?\", \"options\": [\"Schools should completely ban technology.\", \"Students should use AI responsibly.\", \"Teachers should stop teaching.\", \"Students should let AI do all their work.\"], \"correct\": \"1\"}, {\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"What is the main idea?\", \"options\": [\"AI can support education but should be used responsibly.\", \"AI should replace every teacher.\", \"Students should never use technology.\", \"AI is always harmful.\"], \"correct\": \"0\"}, {\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"What does \\\"depend too heavily\\\" most nearly mean?\", \"options\": [\"Use something more than is appropriate\", \"Avoid something completely\", \"Study something carefully\", \"Understand something quickly\"], \"correct\": \"0\"}, {\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"What can be inferred from the passage?\", \"options\": [\"Good use of AI requires students to continue thinking for themselves.\", \"AI can solve every educational problem.\", \"Teachers are no longer necessary.\", \"Students should never use AI tools.\"], \"correct\": \"0\"}]','Published',NULL,'2026-10-08 04:29:35','2026-10-08 12:22:19'),(7,'GRADE 9 — POST-TEST (Technology and Independent Learning)','Post-Test','Frustration',9,'<p>Digital technology has changed the way students find and use information. Instead of depending only on printed books, students can access digital libraries, educational videos, online articles, and interactive learning platforms.</p>\n<p>These resources can make learning more flexible. A student who does not understand a lesson can review a video or read another explanation. Students can also explore topics that interest them beyond what is discussed in class.</p>\n<p>However, having access to information does not automatically mean that students are learning effectively. The internet contains information that may be inaccurate, outdated, or misleading. Students therefore need to evaluate sources before accepting information as true.</p>\n<p>Independent learning also requires discipline. Without a teacher constantly monitoring them, students may become distracted by games, social media, or unrelated websites. Setting goals and managing time can help students use technology productively.</p>\n<p>Technology is therefore most useful when combined with critical thinking and self-discipline. Digital tools can open many opportunities for learning, but students must still take responsibility for how they use them.</p>','[{\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"How has technology changed learning?\", \"options\": [\"It has made information less available.\", \"It has given students access to many digital resources.\", \"It has eliminated the need for books.\", \"It has prevented students from studying independently.\"], \"correct\": \"1\"}, {\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"What can students do if they do not understand a lesson?\", \"options\": [\"Stop studying\", \"Review another explanation or learning resource\", \"Avoid asking questions\", \"Delete their notes\"], \"correct\": \"1\"}, {\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"Why should students evaluate online sources?\", \"options\": [\"Some information online may be inaccurate or misleading.\", \"All online information is correct.\", \"Online information is never useful.\", \"Teachers do not allow online resources.\"], \"correct\": \"0\"}, {\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"What is one challenge of independent learning?\", \"options\": [\"Students may become distracted.\", \"Students cannot access information.\", \"Students have too many teachers.\", \"Students cannot set goals.\"], \"correct\": \"0\"}, {\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"What can help students use technology productively?\", \"options\": [\"Avoiding all digital tools\", \"Setting goals and managing time\", \"Spending more time on social media\", \"Ignoring unreliable information\"], \"correct\": \"1\"}, {\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"What does the passage say about digital resources?\", \"options\": [\"They can provide additional learning opportunities.\", \"They are always accurate.\", \"They should replace teachers.\", \"They are useful only for entertainment.\"], \"correct\": \"0\"}, {\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"What skill is important when using online information?\", \"options\": [\"Critical thinking\", \"Memorization only\", \"Speed reading only\", \"Drawing\"], \"correct\": \"0\"}, {\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"What is the main idea?\", \"options\": [\"Technology makes teachers unnecessary.\", \"Digital technology can support independent learning when used responsibly.\", \"Students should avoid the internet.\", \"Online information is always reliable.\"], \"correct\": \"1\"}, {\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"What does \\\"misleading\\\" most nearly mean?\", \"options\": [\"Likely to give a wrong impression\", \"Easy to understand\", \"Completely accurate\", \"Difficult to access\"], \"correct\": \"0\"}, {\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"What can be inferred?\", \"options\": [\"Students remain responsible for their own learning even when technology is available.\", \"Technology guarantees academic success.\", \"Students do not need critical thinking when using the internet.\", \"Independent learning requires no discipline.\"], \"correct\": \"0\"}]','Published',NULL,'2026-10-08 04:29:35','2026-10-08 12:22:19'),(8,'GRADE 10 — PRE-TEST (Protecting Historical Places)','Pre-Test','Instructional',10,'<p>Historical places provide communities with connections to the past. Old buildings, archaeological sites, monuments, and other cultural locations can help people understand how earlier generations lived.</p>\n<p>In the Philippines, many historical places are found in different regions. Some contain evidence of ancient communities, while others are connected to important events in more recent history. These places can also attract visitors and contribute to local tourism.</p>\n<p>However, historical sites can be damaged by natural disasters, pollution, construction, vandalism, and neglect. Once an important structure or artifact is destroyed, some information about the past may be impossible to recover.</p>\n<p>Preserving historical places requires cooperation. Government agencies can establish rules and provide funding, while local communities can help protect sites and educate visitors. Schools can also encourage young people to learn about their local history.</p>\n<p>Protecting cultural heritage is not simply about preserving old objects. It is about maintaining knowledge and identity for future generations. When communities value their history, they are more likely to protect the places that tell their stories.</p>','[{\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"Why are historical places important?\", \"options\": [\"They provide connections to the past.\", \"They are always modern buildings.\", \"They prevent natural disasters.\", \"They eliminate tourism.\"], \"correct\": \"0\"}, {\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"What can archaeological sites contain?\", \"options\": [\"Evidence of ancient communities\", \"Modern technology only\", \"New buildings\", \"Artificial materials only\"], \"correct\": \"0\"}, {\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"How can historical places benefit communities?\", \"options\": [\"They can contribute to tourism.\", \"They prevent all construction.\", \"They eliminate local businesses.\", \"They stop people from learning.\"], \"correct\": \"0\"}, {\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"Which can damage historical sites?\", \"options\": [\"Proper maintenance\", \"Education\", \"Vandalism\", \"Responsible tourism\"], \"correct\": \"2\"}, {\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"Why is the destruction of an artifact serious?\", \"options\": [\"It may cause information about the past to be lost.\", \"It always improves a historical site.\", \"It makes history easier to study.\", \"It increases the number of artifacts.\"], \"correct\": \"0\"}, {\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"Who can help preserve historical places?\", \"options\": [\"Only tourists\", \"Only students\", \"Government agencies, communities, and schools\", \"Only business owners\"], \"correct\": \"2\"}, {\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"What does cultural heritage include?\", \"options\": [\"Knowledge and places connected to a community\'s past\", \"Only modern buildings\", \"Only tourist attractions\", \"Only natural resources\"], \"correct\": \"0\"}, {\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"What is the main idea?\", \"options\": [\"Historical places should be protected because they preserve cultural knowledge and identity.\", \"Historical places are useful only for tourism.\", \"Communities should replace old buildings with new ones.\", \"Students should avoid learning history.\"], \"correct\": \"0\"}, {\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"What does \\\"preserving\\\" most nearly mean?\", \"options\": [\"Protecting something so it continues to exist\", \"Destroying something\", \"Moving something without care\", \"Ignoring something\"], \"correct\": \"0\"}, {\"type\": \"multichoice\", \"question\": \"What can be inferred?\", \"options\": [\"Young people can play a role in protecting cultural heritage.\", \"Historical preservation is only the government\'s responsibility.\", \"Historical sites have no educational value.\", \"Tourism always destroys historical places.\"], \"correct\": \"0\"}]','Published',NULL,'2026-10-08 04:29:36','2026-10-08 12:20:00'),(9,'GRADE 10 — POST-TEST (Learning from the Past)','Post-Test','Instructional',10,'<p>History is more than a collection of dates and names. It is a record of people\'s experiences, decisions, achievements, and mistakes. Studying history can help communities understand how the present was shaped.</p>\r\n<p>Museums, historical documents, artifacts, and archaeological discoveries are some of the sources used to study the past. Each source provides information, but researchers must examine evidence carefully. A single object or document may not tell the entire story.</p>\r\n<p>Archaeology is particularly useful because it provides physical evidence about earlier societies. Tools, pottery, buildings, and other remains can reveal information about how people lived, worked, traded, and interacted with their environment.</p>\r\n<p>Modern technology has also changed historical research. Digital databases, three-dimensional imaging, and other technologies allow researchers to examine and preserve information more efficiently. Some discoveries can now be studied by people in different parts of the world.</p>\r\n<p>Despite these advances, preserving historical evidence remains important. Future researchers may ask questions that people today cannot yet imagine. Protecting evidence from the past gives future generations an opportunity to make new discoveries and develop a deeper understanding of human history.</p>','[{\"type\":\"multichoice\",\"question\":\"What does history record?\",\"options\":[\"Only dates and names\",\"People\'s experiences, decisions, achievements, and mistakes\",\"Only archaeological objects\",\"Only modern events\"],\"correct\":\"1\"},{\"type\":\"multichoice\",\"question\":\"Which is a source of historical information?\",\"options\":[\"Artifacts\",\"Advertisements only\",\"Weather forecasts\",\"Modern entertainment\"],\"correct\":\"0\"},{\"type\":\"multichoice\",\"question\":\"Why must researchers examine evidence carefully?\",\"options\":[\"One source may not tell the entire story.\",\"Historical sources are always incorrect.\",\"Researchers do not need evidence.\",\"Artifacts have no value.\"],\"correct\":\"0\"},{\"type\":\"multichoice\",\"question\":\"What can archaeology reveal?\",\"options\":[\"How earlier societies lived and worked\",\"Only future events\",\"Modern social media trends\",\"Weather conditions\"],\"correct\":\"0\"},{\"type\":\"multichoice\",\"question\":\"How has technology helped historical research?\",\"options\":[\"It makes evidence disappear.\",\"It allows researchers to examine and preserve information more efficiently.\",\"It prevents researchers from sharing information.\",\"It eliminates the need for evidence.\"],\"correct\":\"1\"},{\"type\":\"multichoice\",\"question\":\"What is one example of modern technology mentioned?\",\"options\":[\"Three-dimensional imaging\",\"Television broadcasting\",\"Online gaming\",\"Digital music\"],\"correct\":\"0\"},{\"type\":\"multichoice\",\"question\":\"Why is preserving historical evidence important?\",\"options\":[\"Future researchers may discover new information from it.\",\"Historical evidence has no future value.\",\"Researchers should avoid studying the past.\",\"Old objects should always be replaced.\"],\"correct\":\"0\"},{\"type\":\"multichoice\",\"question\":\"What is the main idea?\",\"options\":[\"Studying and preserving historical evidence helps people understand the past and make future discoveries.\",\"Technology has made history unnecessary.\",\"Archaeology is the only way to study history.\",\"Historical documents should not be preserved.\"],\"correct\":\"0\"},{\"type\":\"multichoice\",\"question\":\"What does \\\"evidence\\\" mean in the passage?\",\"options\":[\"Information or material used to support knowledge about something\",\"A personal opinion without support\",\"A fictional story\",\"A future prediction\"],\"correct\":\"0\"},{\"type\":\"multichoice\",\"question\":\"What can be inferred from the passage?\",\"options\":[\"New technology can improve historical research, but preserving original evidence remains important.\",\"Technology has completely replaced historical evidence.\",\"Future researchers will have no interest in history.\",\"Archaeological discoveries are no longer useful.\"],\"correct\":\"0\"}]','Published',NULL,'2026-10-08 04:29:36','2026-10-08 12:20:00');
