ntelligence is becoming increasingly common in education. Digital systems can help students practice skills, receive immediate feedback, and access learning materials. For example, an educational system can analyze A student\'s answers and identify areas where the student is having difficulty. A teacher can then use this information to provide more appropriate support. However, artificial intelligence should not completely replace teachers. Teachers understand factors that.\",\"offset\":12700000,\"duration\":311500000},{\"text\":\"Automated systems may not recognize such as a student\'s motivation, are personal circumstances or difficulties outside the classroom. There are also concerns about privacy and responsible IT use of technology. Schools need clear policies to ensure that student information is protected. Artificial intelligence can therefore be useful in education when it is treated as a tool that supports teachers and students rather than as a replacement for human judgment.\",\"offset\":325800000,\"duration\":306300000}],\"diagnostics\":{\"recognizedResults\":2,\"wordEvidence\":134,\"recognizingResults\":119,\"noMatchResults\":0,\"canceledResults\":1,\"audioBytesReceived\":2054400,\"sessionStarted\":true,\"sessionStopped\":true,\"serviceConnected\":true,\"lastRecognizedText\":\"Automated systems may not recognize such as a student\'s motivation, are personal circumstances or difficulties outside the classroom. There are also concerns about privacy and responsible IT use of technology. Schools need clear policies to ensure that student information is protected. Artificial intelligence can therefore be useful in education when it is treated as a tool that supports teachers and students rather than as a replacement for human judgment.\",\"sdkVersion\":\"1.51.2\",\"jsonWordEvidence\":134,\"sdkWordEvidence\":134,\"resultJsonBytes\":133668,\"audioWriterAlive\":false,\"writerFailed\":false},\"error\":null,\"finalSeen\":true,\"doneSeen\":true},\"realtime\":{\"transcript\":\"Artificial intelligence is becoming increasingly common in education. Digital systems can help students practice skills, receive immediate feedback and access learning materials. For example, an educational system can analyze students\' answers and identify areas where the student is having difficulty. A teacher can then use this information to provide more appropriate support. However, artificial intelligence should not completely replace teachers. Teachers understand factors that automated systems may not recognize, such as a student\'s motivational, personal circumstances or difficulties outside the classroom. There are also concerns about privacy and responsible use of technology. Schools need clear policy to ensure that the student information is protected. Artificial intelligence can therefore be useful in education when it is treated as a tool that supports teacher and student rather than as a replacement for human judgment\",\"enabled\":true,\"model\":\"gpt-live-transcribe\",\"requestedModel\":\"gpt-live-transcribe\",\"context\":\"keywords-only\",\"delay\":600,\"vad\":{\"start_threshold\":0.018,\"stop_threshold\":0.012,\"silence_duration_ms\":1500,\"min_speech_ms\":180}},\"pipeline\":{\"realtimeTranscription\":\"gpt-live-transcribe\",\"requestedRealtimeTranscription\":\"gpt-live-transcribe\",\"realtimeTranscriptionContext\":\"keywords-only\",\"realtimeTranscriptionDelay\":600,\"realtimeVAD\":{\"start_threshold\":0.018,\"stop_threshold\":0.012,\"silence_duration_ms\":1500,\"min_speech_ms\":180},\"batchTranscription\":\"disabled\",\"pronunciation\":\"Azure Speech Pronunciation Assessment\",\"comparison\":\"reference passage + OpenAI literal transcript + continuous Azure scripted pronunciation/timing evidence\",\"audioDurationSeconds\":63.718,\"azureStreaming\":true,\"azureReferenceText\":\"hidden-passage\",\"azureFinalSeen\":true,\"azureDoneSeen\":true,\"openaiTranscriptionPasses\":1,\"note\":\"Assessment markup is withheld until Azure finalization